ros/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpyaoxueros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpyaoxueros/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpyaoxueros/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpyaoxueros/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpyaoxueros/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpyaoxueros/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-19T23:01:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T23:01:53Z","body":"I checked the current [Decisions guide](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/decisions) and the generated [OpenAI Python SDK type](https://github.com/openai/openai-python/blob/main/src/openai/types/decision_create_params.py). The guide demonstrates each question's `instructions` as prose, and the SDK types the field as `Required[str]`. This confirms the wire type but does not settle whether a JSON-encoded instruction string is an intended representation.\n\nBefore any code change, could a maintainer confirm the expected format for structured instructions in `OpenAIDecisionsModel` and assign this issue to `@wpyaoxueros` if they want a fix? If plain text is intended, I can prepare a focused request-payload regression and a minimal serializer change. I have not independently run the issue's example or measured model quality, so I won't claim either result.\n\nAI disclosure: OpenAI Codex (GPT-6; reasoning effort not surfaced in this runtime) helped analyze the issue and draft this comment.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/issues/comments/6279244564/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"wpyaoxueros","id":139048865,"node_id":"U_kgDOCEm3oQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139048865?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpyaoxueros","html_url":"https://github.com/wpyaoxueros","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpyaoxueros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpyaoxueros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpyaoxueros/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpyaoxueros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpyaoxueros/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpyaoxueros/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpyaoxueros/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpyaoxueros/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpyaoxueros/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/issues/comments/6293343073","html_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/issues/10647#issuecomment-6293343073","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/issues/10647","id":6293343073,"node_id":"IC_kwDOMMa-Ps8AAAABdxzLYQ","user":{"login":"xixi-box","id":96341168,"node_id":"U_kgDOBb4MsA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96341168?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xixi-box","html_url":"https://github.com/xixi-box","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xixi-box/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xixi-box/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xixi-box/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xixi-box/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xixi-box/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xixi-box/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xixi-box/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xixi-box/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xixi-box/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-20T14:33:43Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T14:33:43Z","body":"Confirmed the divergence from the API contract: `openai.types.decision_create_params` types `instructions` as a plain `str`, and the [Decisions guide](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/decisions) shows prose — while `_instructions()` → `_text()` JSON-encodes any non-string `JsonValue`, so internal keys (`field`, `goal`, `premise`, `background`, `yes`/`no`) end up inside the instructions string.\n\nIf the intent is to keep the labelled structure internally but render plain prose on the wire, I'd propose `_instructions()` rendering the labelled parts as text — goal, then context/premise, then the question, then what yes and no mean — without the internal key names. The snapshots in `tests/models/test_openai_decisions.py` would move accordingly, and the A/B on the labelled set (as suggested in the report) would tell whether prose closes the gap vs `typesafe`.\n\nSince #9634 introduced the encoding deliberately, I'd want a maintainer's nod on the intended wire format before changing it — happy to prepare the change once that's settled.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/issues/comments/6293343073/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"xixi-box","id":96341168,"node_id":"U_kgDOBb4MsA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96341168?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xixi-box","html_url":"https://github.com/xixi-box","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xixi-box/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xixi-box/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https: